by the Hebrews with strictest reference to the interposition of God, and as a method of ascertaining the divine will (Prov. 16:33), and in serious cases of doubt (Esther 3:7).","verses":34,"father":"Haran","mother":"","v":[4,5]},{"id":"sarah_2473","name":"Sarah","also":"Sarai, Sara","summary":"Princess, the wife and at the same time the half-sister of Abraham (Gen. 11:29; 20:12). This name was given to her at the time that it was announced to Abraham that she should be the mother of the promised child.","verses":48,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[5,11,17]},{"id":"pharaoh_2331","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh of the Exodus was probably Menephtah I., the fourteenth and eldest surviving son of Rameses II. He resided at Zoan, where he had the various interviews with Moses and Aaron recorded in the book of Exodus.","verses":138,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"pharaoh_2328","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh who was on the throne when Abram went down into Egypt (Gen. 12:10-20) was probably one of the Hyksos, or “shepherd kings.” The Egyptians called the nomad tribes of Syria Shasu, “plunderers,” their king or chief Hyk, and hence the name of those invaders who conquered the native kings and established a strong government, with Zoan or Tanis as their capital.","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15,17,18,20]}],"places":[{"id":"haran_527","name":"Haran","kind":"City","lat":36.86,"lon":39.03139,"summary":"Heb. haran, i.e., “parched;” or probably from the Accadian charana, meaning “a road.” A celebrated city of Western Asia, now Harran, where Abram remained, after he left Ur of the Chaldees, till his father Terah died (Gen. 11:31, 32), when he continued his journey into the land of Canaan.","verses":10,"v":[4,5]},{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[5]},{"id":"moreh_817","name":"Moreh","kind":"","lat":32.21369,"lon":35.2818,"summary":"A Canaanite probably who inhabited the district south of Shechem, between Mounts Ebal and Gerizim, and gave his name to the “plain” there (Gen. 12:6).","verses":2,"v":[6]},{"id":"shechem_1069","name":"Shechem","kind":"City","lat":32.22111,"lon":35.25444,"summary":"A city in Samaria (Gen. 33:18), called also Sichem (12:6), Sychem (Acts 7:16). It stood in the narrow sheltered valley between Ebal on the north and Gerizim on the south, these mountains at their base being only some 500 yards apart.","verses":40,"v":[6]},{"id":"ai_36","name":"Ai","kind":"City","lat":31.91668,"lon":35.26158,"summary":"One of the royal cities of the Canaanites (Josh. 10:1; Gen. 12:8; 13:3). It was the scene of Joshua’s defeat, and afterwards of his victory.","verses":31,"v":[8]},{"id":"bethel_202","name":"Bethel","kind":"","lat":31.93054,"lon":35.22103,"summary":"A place in Central Palestine, about 10 miles north of Jerusalem, at the head of the pass of Michmash and Ai. It was originally the royal Canaanite city of Luz (Gen. 28:19).","verses":62,"v":[8]},{"id":"negeb_885","name":"Negeb","kind":"Region","lat":30.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Heb. Negeb, that arid district to the south of Palestine through which lay the caravan route from Central Palestine to Egypt (Gen. 12:9; 13:1, 3; 46:1-6).","verses":36,"v":[9]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[10,11,12,14]}],"events":[{"id":"abraham_enters_canaan_71","title":"Abraham enters Canaan","year":-1921,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 11:31–12:9. People: Abraham, Lot, Sarah. Place: Canaan, Haran, Shechem, Moreh.","v":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9]},{"id":"abrahamic_covenant_72","title":"Abrahamic Covenant",